t null and names no road, so the 200 m corroboration test is undecidable on the record and that clause is unavailable, not exculpatory. There is no billing-integrity refund either: the airport surcharge is 0.00, correctly, because this trip ends at Changi rather than originating there, and no ERP or toll line was charged (EV-FARE-00108). The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00108-01, status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and changes nothing, since no party asserts an external traffic cause and it is not invoked against the driver. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (0 flags over 402 trips in 90 days), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral arises; and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires - the trip identifiers all match, the trace is unbroken (206 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps), the amended optimal is stored and non-null, every fare line reconciles, and nothing is invoked against a missing artifact. The ruling rests on EV-GPS-00108 and EV-TRIP-00108, both at weight 1.0. The outcome is NO_ACTION: the metered charge of $33.77 stands as charged and nothing is refunded."
